WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:10.033
A rep gets a few minutes with an HCP. And most of them rehearse on the real thing.

2
00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:17.480
Role play pulls a manager off the road. It never happens often enough, and no two sessions are the same.

3
00:00:18.233 --> 00:00:22.543
So we built CallReady. A safe place to practise first.

4
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:34.977
Pick the doctor, and where they sit on the adoption ladder. Then talk it through, out loud, with a realistic Australian HCP who's busy, asks questions, and pushes back.

5
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:40.592
Every doctor carries a hidden concern. The rep has to draw it out.

6
00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:44.833
Minutes later, a clear score, on screen.

7
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:59.027
Seven criteria by default. Discovery, unmet need, the hidden concern, approved claims, PBS, adverse event reporting, and gaining commitment. Or set your own.

8
00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:05.279
And it doesn't just score. It names the moment that went wrong, and the line that worked.

9
00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:13.373
In the car park on a phone, at cycle launch, or on day one. Practice that fits around the field week.

10
00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:22.832
Managers get reps who've already handled the objection. Trainers get consistent role play for every rep, without pulling anyone off the road.

11
00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:31.143
The HCP is fictional. The practice is real. CallReady. Practise the call before the call.

